A||N||17||AusFiero||My new daily driver.||||6||
Z||000000||AusFiero||09-30-2001||02:19 AM||||Well ok it isn't a Fiero. I figured I might as well ahve the best of both worlds. The Fiero is getting fixed and I bought this to get around in on a daily basis. So no, I haven't totally defected to the MR2 camp  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Was too good to pass up for the price. Is a non turbo but I bought a rear cut of a turbo model 2 days later. Engine swap in progress Tuesday. But not by me, I haven't got enough time. So then it will have ABS, Traction Control, Limited Slip Diff and a bloody good amount of power to boot. <P>I will spend my time getting the Fiero and Stage 2 parts back on track after the fire. <P>Certainly different to the Fiero. both have their good and bad points.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/MR2001.jpg"> <P><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||6
Z||000001||fierobaby||09-30-2001||02:21 AM||||wow Aus! nice... not so sure I like silver though... I'm more of a blue/red/green girl but still pretty||||reg||1
Z||000002||frontal lobe||09-30-2001||03:25 AM||||Hey, nothing to be embarrassed about.  Toyota reliability.  Good gas mileage.  You could do a lot worse for a daily driver.  Good find.<P>Details?  Year?  Mileage?   Are those t-tops?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Leper||09-30-2001||03:43 AM||||I'm not a person that hates MR2's, but I never knew how ugly they were until just now. I thought that gen2 cars were supposed to be the good looking ones.<BR>After you get the Fiero body kit done, please help that car out!||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||09-30-2001||03:43 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by frontal lobe:<BR><B>Hey, nothing to be embarrassed about.  Toyota reliability.  Good gas mileage.  You could do a lot worse for a daily driver.  Good find.<P>Details?  Year?  Mileage?   Are those t-tops?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It has all the bells and whistles. Electric everything. 10 stacker CD, yes, t-tops. I cant have 2 seats and no t-tops (c: Fiero spoilt me on that 1. It has 130,000 KMS (about 75,000 Miles). The Japanese turbo rear cut I bought has 68,000 KMS (about 40,000 miles) on it. The Japanese turbo models are also more powerful than the Australian or USA models. Finally it is a 1991 model. The rear cut I bought is a 1994 model. I paid 55% of a dealers price because it needs new paint. Colour I am trying to decide.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula||09-30-2001||10:53 AM||||and the question of the day......<P>is the mr2 as wide as the fiero?  Do you think the nose would fit on the fiero (for a shogun mr2 nose)?||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||09-30-2001||11:33 AM||||Looks great!  Watch out, you might start liking it more than your Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The Fieros are a tad lower and wider, and you do sit lower... but the MR2 is really comfortable inside, and there is enough room behind the seats for subs on those little storage bins back there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  ||||reg||10
Z||000007||RoadRocket||09-30-2001||11:53 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leper:<BR><B>I thought that gen2 cars were supposed to be the good looking ones.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Gen2 <B>ARE</B> better looking than the Gen1 MR2! Have you ever seen a Gen1? Looks like a prop from Star Wars.<P>I looked at one at the same time I looked at the Fiero, liked the Fiero <u>much</u> better.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Ed Dana<BR>88 Coupe.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||09-30-2001||01:10 PM||||So, how does it compare to the Fiero, Aus?  Handling, power?  I've thought about getting a MKII Turbo cuz they are attractive cars and have the same things that I like about the Fiero.  I don't because I figure any money spent on an MR2 would be better spent on my Fiero.  :/  <P>But you can get a late model MR2, the youngest Fieros are 13 years old.  So for daily drivers, it's not a bad choice.  I keep thinking I should sell my 99 Grand Am so I can spend more money on my Fiero!  ||||reg||5
Z||000009||Doni Hagan||09-30-2001||02:27 PM||||Hi. This is kinda O/T in itself but I posted something in General Chat for ya....<P>New toy, huh?  A friend here has one (lowered and totally "riced" out) and they're a blast to drive. Like you said they're different from Fieros but still fun in their own way. He calls it his "point and squirt" car. <P>||||reg||6
Z||000010||Leper||09-30-2001||03:55 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by RoadRocket:<BR><B> Gen2 <I>ARE</I> better looking than the Gen1 MR2! Have you ever seen a Gen1? Looks like a prop from Star Wars.<P>I looked at one at the same time I looked at the Fiero, liked the Fiero <u>much</u> better.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I know the 1st gen cars are bad, but Aus's car is the first good look I've had at a 2nd gen. (I've only seen 1 in real life, and I only caught a glimpse.) From how everyone talks about them, I thought that they would look more exotic than that and less like an average Japanese econobox.<p>[This message has been edited by Leper (edited 09-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tonker||09-30-2001||04:35 PM||||Aus, It's gorgeous!! I love 'em!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||AusFiero||09-30-2001||07:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula88:<BR><B>So, how does it compare to the Fiero, Aus?  Handling, power?  I've thought about getting a MKII Turbo cuz they are attractive cars and have the same things that I like about the Fiero.  I don't because I figure any money spent on an MR2 would be better spent on my Fiero.  :/  <P>But you can get a late model MR2, the youngest Fieros are 13 years old.  So for daily drivers, it's not a bad choice.  I keep thinking I should sell my 99 Grand Am so I can spend more money on my Fiero!  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It handles like it is on rails. I thought the Fiero was good but man this takes some beating. Power wise as a non turbo it is pretty good as it has the same horsepower as the Fiero. I think the V6 has a little more torque. Once the turbo engine goes in next week it is going to be a vey fun car to drive. I definately like the better brakes. <P>Probably in all fairness the only thing the Fiero has over it is looks. As it is a later model car it is naturally better in most other respects. Not many people look at this car but they gape in awe at my Fiero. So for a daily driver with plenty of power it is a ton of fun. When I feel like posin I will get the Fiero out to play with  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I am going to do both up so when the Fiero is back on the road I may even sell this one as I can make a very healthy profit on it. But on the other hand having a daily driver with cheap maintainance and parts is good for a change.  <P>||||reg||3
Z||000013||Phil||09-30-2001||08:04 PM||||If you had said "I just found this rebody kit for a Fiero" you would have had at least 25 posts on "How do I get one?" or "How much?" and assorted wow and cool. But now you get "MR2?"<BR>Just an observation:||||reg||1
Z||000014||FieroMaster88||09-30-2001||08:12 PM||||Looks good man!  You have to let us know if the nose will fit on a Fiero. I want to find an aftermarked nose for a MR2 and put it on my Fiero, but not if it wont fit! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jamessig.jpg">              <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>Not your ordinary 88 coupe!||||reg||14
Z||000015||Raydar||09-30-2001||10:11 PM||||Aus,<P>I like it! I would change the wheels, but that's just me. <P>I like MR2s. Always have. Almost bought a new one in 85. Cornered like a slot car. Only thing I ever drove that felt anything like it was a Lotus Europa. <BR>...Then I saw the 85 GT, and heard that V-6 rumble. Sold!<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000016||sqoach||10-01-2001||03:05 PM||||Hey, that's not too bad. I've always liked the front of the 2nd gen MR2. Kinda reminds me of the NSX  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><BR>The t-tops are a plus.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">            <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*SOLD*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000017||MinnGreenGT||10-01-2001||04:22 PM||||AUS- nice daily driver.  I'll admit that if I could find one for cheap (especially a J-spec)- I'd certainly use it as a daily driver too!  <P>If you don't know the reference people keep asking about the front fascia... someone stated some time ago that an aftermarket MR2 (2nd Gen) front end would "nearly bolt up to the Fiero"  -hence people asking. Just explaining in case you missed that in a post somewhere along the way.<P>BTW: you at all interested in selling a RH Drive Fiero conversion from one of your donor cars?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
